title: don't show view-ancestors in a node's containers
pid: 0631c609-85f0-4587-b062-5c1a9f6e38fd
body: |2-
  I often see a view like this:
  ````
    * a
    ** b
    *** these contain it
    **** a // redundant
    **** c
  ```
  That line marked redundant does not need to exist.

  This will be especially helpful in the diff view, which currently draws
  a lot of "its containers changed" folders, most of which have such single
  redundant children; they would instead have no such folder.

  As part of this, we should relabel those folder nodes:
    these contain it       -> these also contain it
    its containers changed -> its other containers changed
